## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
Top-level: `stageW 640 · stageH 440 · tileW 118 · tileH 118 · tileY 92 · tileGapPx 150 (centre-to-centre offset from stage centre ±) · frameWidthPx 13 · tagAngleDeg -4 · tagFontPx 11 · nameFontPx 19 · rowLabelFontPx 15 · rowNumFontPx 27 · numeralFontPx 30 · squareSizePx 13 · squarePitchPx 19 · gridCols 5 · iconFraction 0.6 · tIconMs 0 · iconHoldMs 1200 · iconOutDurMs 600 · tTilesMs 1800 · tileDurMs 2200 · tileStaggerMs 500 · tFreeMs 5000 · freeDurMs 600 · tFrameMs 8500 · frameDurMs 1000 · tTagMs 12500 · tagDurMs 500 · tSquaresMs 15000 · squareFadeMs 400 · squareStaggerMs 55 · holdMs 9500 · easeIcon/easeTile/easeFade/easeFrame/easeSquares all "easeInOut" · palette {ground #f4f1ea, tile #46585c, tileName #dfe9e6, silhouette #3a4c50, frame #c96f4a, tagBg #c4453c, tagAlt #2f6f79, bannerBg #c4453c, bannerAlt #2f6f79, iconTop #d2691e, iconBottom #33484d, square #141414, ink #2b2b2b, muted #6d6d6d, enslavedNum #c96f4a} · fontFamily "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif" · clauseText "Three-fifths clause" · enslavedLabel "Enslaved people:" · freeLabel "Free people:"`.
Nested: `states[2]` — `{label, enslaved, free, electors, tagged, silhouette}`: Virginia {347000, 539000, 21, true, simplified polygon points} · Pennsylvania {1700, 601000, 15, false, simplified polygon points}. Silhouette polygons are coarse CONFIG point lists (a generic state-ish outline per tile), priced as decoration-level geometry — the technique is the count board, not cartography.
Derived (named, not stored): tile x positions (stage centre ∓ tileGapPx, order = states order BUT entry order is entryOrder per state — see below) · entry order: Pennsylvania enters first, Virginia second — carried as `states[].enterIdx` (PA 0, VA 1) so the stagger binds to data, not position · square positions (gridCols columns, rows = ceil(electors/gridCols), flanking outward from each tile) · numeral text = String(electors) · formatted counts = comma-grouping of the CONFIG numbers · **phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** tTiles ≥ icon exit end · tFree ≥ last tile end · tFrame ≥ free end · tTag ≥ frame end · tSquares ≥ tag end — a CONFIG violating the order is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped. **Count assertion (A9.3):** source counts — states 2, electors 21 + 15 = 36 — vs built counts printed by the harness; mismatch halts.
Complete-at: squares last = tSquaresMs + (maxElectors−1)·squareStaggerMs + squareFadeMs = 15000 + 20·55 + 400 = 16500… — NOTE: census CP8 (16000 ms) shows squares mid-landing and CP9 (18000) complete; 16500 complete is inside that bracket ✓. durationMs = completeAt + holdMs = 16500 + 9500 = 26000 (window length; holdMs set 9500 so the board holds to the window end under the departure in §2.3).

### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG tiles + square grids (chosen):** one SVG scene; a person-icon group (circle + body path split at the CONFIG fraction into two fills), banner rect + text, per-state tile group (rect + silhouette polygon + name), frame rect (tagged state only), tag group (rotated rect + text), two population text rows per state, per-state square grid of rects + numeral text — all geometry/opacity from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). HTML divs — SVG gives exact geometry for harness receipts at less code.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: segment-anchored, build 0 ms = source 305000 ms. **Departure table:** ONE departure — SB-H portrait coda (census CP11–CP12, 22000–24000 ms): a photographic painting slides up and covers the board. DEFERRED with reason: photographic content cannot be recreated by code/generated construction without specimen media or tracing (§6.1 refusal class), and it is not the count-board technique — it is the narration's payoff image. The build instead HOLDS the completed scoreboard from completeAt (16500 ms) to durationMs (26000 ms); CP13 (26000 ms) is the next technique (T220) and asserts nothing about T219. All other checkpoints map 1:1.
Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant):
- CP0 zero/icon: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tIconMs)` → 0 ms: iconP=1, banner present, tiles scale 0, squares 0. (Zero-state anchor for tiles/squares, guards cmd 8.)
- P1 icon exit: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.iconHoldMs + CONFIG.iconOutDurMs)` → 1800 ms: iconP=0.
- C@2000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 2000)`: PA (enterIdx 0) tileP = easeTile(clamp01((2000−tTilesMs)/tileDurMs)) > 0; VA (enterIdx 1) tileP = 0 (its staggered start = tTilesMs + tileStaggerMs = 2300 > 2000). Order receipt.
- P2 tiles complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tTilesMs + CONFIG.tileStaggerMs + CONFIG.tileDurMs)` → 4500 ms: both tileP=1, freeP=0.
- C@6000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 6000)`: freeP=1 both states, enslavedP=0, frameP=0, squares 0.
- C@8000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 8000)`: state identical in the priced fields to C@6000 (hold).
- P3 frame mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tFrameMs + CONFIG.frameDurMs/2)` → 9000 ms: frameP=0.5, enslavedP=0.5.
- C@10000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 10000)`: frameP=1, enslavedP=1, tagP=0, squares 0.
- C@12000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 12000)`: tagP=0 (zero-state anchor for the tag), squares 0, frameP=1.
- C@14000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 14000)`: tagP=1, squares 0 (zero-state anchor for squares).
- P4 squares mid: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSquaresMs + 1000)` → 16000 ms: 0 < VA squaresVisible < 21 and 0 < PA squaresVisible < 15 (fractional visibility sum), numerals opacity > 0.
- C@18000: `stateAt(CONFIG, 18000)`: VA squares = 21 exactly, PA squares = 15 exactly (full-opacity count), numerals = "21"/"15".
- P5 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 500)` fully equal to `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs)`. durationMs = 26000 ✓ = window.

### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.webm at 304.5–331.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p+AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T219 exposed); (3) build comparison.html (shared controls, video.currentTime − 0.5 s handle offset → build ms, labels as charged, phone stacking @media ≤560px); (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3.
